
  <sn><md>### Installing Rclone in Linux

On Ubuntu/Debian, there are several ways to install Rclone. The easiest is the **official installation script**.


**Install Rclone**

```bash
sudo -v ; curl https://rclone.org/install.sh | sudo bash
```

Then check the installation:

```bash
rclone version
```

You should see something similar to:

```text
rclone v1.xx.x
os/version: linux
```
